The trame documentation provides a catalog of the widgets and applications of
the trame ecosystem. At the beginning of the internship, this catalog consisted
of a single manually maintained page, which did not scale with the growing
ecosystem and did not help users discover applications. It was reworked into two
automatically generated pages, the widget catalog and the application catalog
(\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/899}), from which the screenshot in \cref{fig:trame-widgets}
is taken.

\insertfigure{assets/images/trame-widgets}{width=\textwidth}{Screenshot of the
trame widgets catalog}{fig:trame-widgets}

The catalogs no longer need to be edited by hand: their content is fetched from
the GitHub API for Kitware-owned repositories carrying the \texttt{trame}
topic, complemented by a curated list of community repositories that overrides
or completes the fetched metadata. The pages provide a search bar, filtering by
multiple tags, and sorting by various metrics, such as the number of stars or
the date of the last commit. The documentation build is scheduled to run daily,
so newly created widgets and applications appear automatically.

Following this initial development, the catalogs were improved and kept stable
through a series of maintenance pull requests. The URL management of renamed
external repositories was hardened and unmatched URLs now report an explicit
error (\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/901}). The interface was refined, changing the
emoji marking community repositories and making a click on a topic toggle its
filter (\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/902}). The merging of the curated data with the
fetched data, which caused some applications to disappear from the application
catalog, was corrected and logging was added (\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/903}). The
preview images, which were fetched from URLs only valid for a short time, are
now downloaded and served by the documentation site itself, also improving
their loading time (\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/905}). Finally, repositories that no
longer existed made the builds fail; they are now skipped with a warning,
keeping the build green (\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/908}).